Comparing wedding AV rental quotes is a different job from vetting one provider you have already shortlisted. This page is about holding two or more quotes side by side and spotting what one discloses that the other leaves out, before you have committed to anyone. If you already have a provider in mind and want the questions to ask before booking them, see our [questions to ask a wedding rental company](/blog/questions-to-ask-wedding-rental-companies/) guide instead. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

A comparable wedding AV quote states nine things plainly: the guest capacity the sound system is rated for, what the sound, lighting and microphones actually are, whether a technician is on site, whether transport, setup and teardown are bundled into the price or billed separately, and whether the net price and VAT are shown apart. Below is a checklist for what to look for, then Malaga Event Gear's own [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) and [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) itemized line by line, so you can write any other quote into the same rows and see where it goes vague.

## Key Highlights

---

- Nine line items make a wedding AV quote genuinely comparable: guest capacity, sound, lighting, microphones, technician, transport, setup and teardown, net price, and VAT.
- MEG's Eco Pack and Wedding Pack are itemized below as a working reference, real figures, not placeholder rows.
- A lower price on a competing quote can simply mean a lower guest capacity or no technician, not a lower cost for the same coverage.
- Getting more than one quote before booking is worth doing precisely so you have something to hold this checklist against.

## What an Itemized AV Quote Should Actually Show

A quote you can genuinely compare against another one states these nine things without you having to ask:

- **Guest capacity.** A number the sound system is rated for, not a venue size description.
- **Sound system.** What the speakers actually are, not just "PA system."
- **Microphones.** How many and what kind, wired or wireless.
- **Lighting.** What it is, since "lighting included" covers very different setups.
- **Technician, included or not.** Whether anyone is on site running the equipment during the event, or whether it is delivered, installed, tested and left running.
- **Transport.** Whether getting the gear to your venue is part of the price or a separate line item.
- **Setup and teardown.** Whether installation and pickup are included, or billed on top.
- **Net price.** The package cost before tax, stated as a number, not a vague "starting from" figure.
- **VAT.** Whether the price shown already includes Spain's 21 percent VAT, and whether the final quote breaks the two apart.

