## MEG's Own Quote, Itemized

Here is what a comparable AV quote looks like when every one of those nine items is actually filled in, using MEG's own two wedding sized packages. Write any other provider's quote into a third column against these same rows and see what they leave blank.

| Line item | Eco Pack | Wedding Pack |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guest capacity | Up to 50 | Up to 80 |
| Sound system | 2 active speakers with stands | High end active PA acoustic system |
| Microphones | 1 wired dynamic microphone | Wireless microphones for speeches |
| Lighting | 2 light bars with RGBW LED spotlights | Fairy lights and warm LED strings |
| Technician on site | Not included, self run after setup | Included, throughout the event |
| Transport | Included | Included |
| Setup and teardown | Included | Included |
| Net price (ex VAT) | 290 euros | 650 euros |
| VAT | Not included, +21% shown separately on final quote | Not included, +21% shown separately on final quote |

Both packages bake transport, setup and teardown into the listed price rather than billing them as separate line items, which is worth confirming on any other quote you receive, since it is often priced apart elsewhere.

## Why Two Quotes for "the Same Package" Land at Different Prices

When two AV quotes look similar on the surface but land at different numbers, the honest reason is almost always one of four things: a different guest capacity rating, whether a technician is included, whether VAT is already in the number or gets added afterward, and whether delivery and setup are bundled into the price or charged separately. It is rarely a vague difference in "quality." If a provider cannot point to which of those four moved the price, ask them directly rather than assuming the higher number is simply better equipment.

## Red Flags in a Vague Quote

A few things are worth treating as a reason to ask more questions before booking, not a normal industry quirk:

- No guest capacity number stated anywhere, just a venue size description.
- No mention of whether VAT is included in the quoted price.
- "Sound system" or "AV package" with nothing describing what the speakers or lighting actually are.
- No statement of who, if anyone, is present during the event running the equipment.
- Furniture, tenting or decor bundled into an "AV package." Audio visual and event decor are typically separate trades, so a quote that blends the two into one number is harder to compare against a quote from a company that only does one of them.

## Is the Cheapest Quote Always the Best One

Not necessarily, and this is why the checklist above matters more than the total at the bottom of the page. A lower number can be covering less, not costing less for the same thing. Getting quotes from more than one company before booking is worth doing for exactly this reason: it gives you something concrete to hold this checklist against, rather than judging a single number in isolation.

